# Filament v4 Development Rules

## Overview
This document contains best practices and conventions for developing Laravel applications with Filament v4.

## General Principles

### Code Organization
- Follow Laravel's standard directory structure
- Keep Filament resources, pages, and widgets organized in their respective directories
- Use namespaces consistently: `App\Filament\Resources`, `App\Filament\Pages`, `App\Filament\Widgets`
- Group related functionality together (e.g., custom actions, filters)

### Naming Conventions
- Resources: Singular, PascalCase (e.g., `UserResource`, `PostResource`)
- Pages: Descriptive, PascalCase (e.g., `Dashboard`, `Settings`)
- Widgets: Descriptive with "Widget" suffix (e.g., `StatsOverviewWidget`)
- Custom Actions: Descriptive, PascalCase (e.g., `ExportAction`, `PublishAction`)
- Form fields: snake_case matching database columns
- Relationship methods: camelCase following Laravel conventions

## Resource Development

### Resource Structure
```php
class PostResource extends Resource
{
    protected static ?string $model = Post::class;
    
    protected static ?string $navigationIcon = 'heroicon-o-document-text';
    
    protected static ?string $navigationGroup = 'Content';
    
    protected static ?int $navigationSort = 1;
    
    public static function form(Form $form): Form
    {
        return $form->schema([
            // Form fields
        ]);
    }
    
    public static function table(Table $table): Table
    {
        return $table
            ->columns([
                // Table columns
            ])
            ->filters([
                // Filters
            ])
            ->actions([
                // Row actions
            ])
            ->bulkActions([
                // Bulk actions
            ]);
    }
    
    public static function getRelations(): array
    {
        return [
            // Relation managers
        ];
    }
    
    public static function getPages(): array
    {
        return [
            'index' => Pages\ListPosts::route('/'),
            'create' => Pages\CreatePost::route('/create'),
            'edit' => Pages\EditPost::route('/{record}/edit'),
        ];
    }
}
```

### Form Best Practices
- Use appropriate field types (TextInput, Textarea, Select, etc.)
- Implement validation rules directly on fields using `->required()`, `->email()`, etc.
- Group related fields using `Section` or `Fieldset` components
- Use `Grid` and `Split` for responsive layouts
- Leverage `->relationship()` for foreign key fields
- Use `->reactive()` for fields that affect other fields
- Implement `->afterStateUpdated()` for real-time field interactions
- Use `->hidden()` or `->visible()` with closures for conditional fields
- Apply `->columnSpan()` for flexible grid layouts

```php
Forms\Components\Section::make('Basic Information')
    ->schema([
        Forms\Components\TextInput::make('title')
            ->required()
            ->maxLength(255)
            ->live(onBlur: true)
            ->afterStateUpdated(fn ($state, callable $set) => 
                $set('slug', Str::slug($state))
            ),
        
        Forms\Components\TextInput::make('slug')
            ->required()
            ->unique(ignoreRecord: true),
        
        Forms\Components\Select::make('status')
            ->options([
                'draft' => 'Draft',
                'published' => 'Published',
                'archived' => 'Archived',
            ])
            ->default('draft')
            ->required(),
    ])
    ->columns(2);
```

### Table Best Practices
- Use appropriate column types (TextColumn, BooleanColumn, ImageColumn, etc.)
- Implement searchable columns with `->searchable()`
- Make columns sortable with `->sortable()`
- Use `->toggleable()` for optional columns
- Group related columns logically
- Add helpful badges with `BadgeColumn` for status fields
- Use `->limit()` for long text columns
- Implement custom column rendering with `->formatStateUsing()`
- Add filters for common search criteria
- Use bulk actions for batch operations

```php
Tables\Columns\TextColumn::make('title')
    ->searchable()
    ->sortable()
    ->limit(50)
    ->tooltip(fn ($record) => $record->title),

Tables\Columns\BadgeColumn::make('status')
    ->colors([
        'warning' => 'draft',
        'success' => 'published',
        'danger' => 'archived',
    ]),

Tables\Columns\IconColumn::make('is_featured')
    ->boolean()
    ->sortable(),

Tables\Columns\TextColumn::make('created_at')
    ->dateTime()
    ->sortable()
    ->toggleable(),
```

### Filters
- Use `SelectFilter` for categorical data
- Implement `TernaryFilter` for boolean fields
- Use `Filter` with custom forms for complex filtering
- Group related filters
- Add `->multiple()` for multi-select filters

```php
Tables\Filters\SelectFilter::make('status')
    ->options([
        'draft' => 'Draft',
        'published' => 'Published',
        'archived' => 'Archived',
    ])
    ->multiple(),

Tables\Filters\TernaryFilter::make('is_featured')
    ->label('Featured')
    ->boolean()
    ->trueLabel('Only featured')
    ->falseLabel('Not featured')
    ->native(false),

Tables\Filters\Filter::make('created_at')
    ->form([
        Forms\Components\DatePicker::make('created_from'),
        Forms\Components\DatePicker::make('created_until'),
    ])
    ->query(function (Builder $query, array $data): Builder {
        return $query
            ->when(
                $data['created_from'],
                fn (Builder $query, $date): Builder => $query->whereDate('created_at', '>=', $date),
            )
            ->when(
                $data['created_until'],
                fn (Builder $query, $date): Builder => $query->whereDate('created_at', '<=', $date),
            );
    }),
```

### Actions
- Keep action logic in dedicated action classes when complex
- Use `->requiresConfirmation()` for destructive actions
- Add `->form()` for actions requiring input
- Implement `->successNotification()` for user feedback
- Use `->after()` for post-action logic
- Group related actions logically

```php
Tables\Actions\Action::make('publish')
    ->icon('heroicon-o-check')
    ->requiresConfirmation()
    ->action(fn (Post $record) => $record->publish())
    ->successNotification(
        Notification::make()
            ->success()
            ->title('Post published')
            ->body('The post has been published successfully.')
    )
    ->visible(fn (Post $record) => $record->isDraft()),
```

## Relation Managers

### Best Practices
- Create relation managers for important relationships
- Use appropriate form and table configurations
- Implement proper authorization checks
- Add custom actions when needed
- Use `->recordTitleAttribute()` for better UX

```php
class CommentsRelationManager extends RelationManager
{
    protected static string $relationship = 'comments';
    
    protected static ?string $recordTitleAttribute = 'content';
    
    public function form(Form $form): Form
    {
        return $form
            ->schema([
                Forms\Components\Textarea::make('content')
                    ->required()
                    ->maxLength(1000),
                
                Forms\Components\Toggle::make('is_approved')
                    ->default(false),
            ]);
    }
    
    public function table(Table $table): Table
    {
        return $table
            ->columns([
                Tables\Columns\TextColumn::make('content')
                    ->limit(50),
                Tables\Columns\IconColumn::make('is_approved')
                    ->boolean(),
                Tables\Columns\TextColumn::make('created_at')
                    ->dateTime(),
            ])
            ->filters([
                Tables\Filters\TernaryFilter::make('is_approved'),
            ])
            ->headerActions([
                Tables\Actions\CreateAction::make(),
            ])
            ->actions([
                Tables\Actions\EditAction::make(),
                Tables\Actions\DeleteAction::make(),
            ])
            ->bulkActions([
                Tables\Actions\BulkActionGroup::make([
                    Tables\Actions\DeleteBulkAction::make(),
                ]),
            ]);
    }
}
```

## Custom Pages

### Dashboard Development
- Use widgets effectively for data visualization
- Implement filtering options for date ranges
- Keep dashboards performant with proper query optimization
- Use caching for expensive calculations
- Make dashboards responsive

```php
class Dashboard extends Page
{
    protected static ?string $navigationIcon = 'heroicon-o-home';
    
    protected static string $view = 'filament.pages.dashboard';
    
    public function getHeaderWidgets(): array
    {
        return [
            StatsOverviewWidget::class,
            RecentOrdersWidget::class,
        ];
    }
    
    protected function getHeaderWidgetsColumns(): int | array
    {
        return 3;
    }
}
```

### Custom Pages with Forms
- Use `InteractsWithForms` trait
- Implement `getFormSchema()` method
- Handle form submission properly
- Add proper validation
- Provide user feedback

```php
use Filament\Forms\Concerns\InteractsWithForms;
use Filament\Forms\Contracts\HasForms;

class Settings extends Page implements HasForms
{
    use InteractsWithForms;
    
    protected static string $view = 'filament.pages.settings';
    
    public ?array $data = [];
    
    public function mount(): void
    {
        $this->form->fill();
    }
    
    protected function getFormSchema(): array
    {
        return [
            Forms\Components\TextInput::make('site_name')
                ->required(),
            Forms\Components\Textarea::make('site_description'),
        ];
    }
    
    public function submit(): void
    {
        $data = $this->form->getState();
        
        // Save settings logic
        
        Notification::make()
            ->success()
            ->title('Settings saved')
            ->send();
    }
}
```

## Widgets

### Types and Usage
- **Stats Widgets**: Display key metrics
- **Chart Widgets**: Visualize data trends
- **Table Widgets**: Show data tables
- Keep queries optimized
- Use caching for expensive data
- Make widgets responsive

```php
class StatsOverviewWidget extends StatsOverviewWidget
{
    protected function getStats(): array
    {
        return [
            Stat::make('Total Users', User::count())
                ->description('32k increase')
                ->descriptionIcon('heroicon-m-arrow-trending-up')
                ->color('success')
                ->chart([7, 2, 10, 3, 15, 4, 17]),
                
            Stat::make('Bounce rate', '21%')
                ->description('7% increase')
                ->descriptionIcon('heroicon-m-arrow-trending-down')
                ->color('danger'),
                
            Stat::make('Average time on page', '3:12')
                ->description('3% increase')
                ->descriptionIcon('heroicon-m-arrow-trending-up')
                ->color('success'),
        ];
    }
}
```

## Authorization

### Policy Integration
- Implement Laravel policies for resources
- Use policy methods: `viewAny`, `view`, `create`, `update`, `delete`, `forceDelete`, `restore`
- Add custom authorization methods when needed
- Check permissions in actions and pages

```php
// In Resource
public static function canViewAny(): bool
{
    return auth()->user()->can('view_posts');
}

// In Action
Tables\Actions\DeleteAction::make()
    ->visible(fn (Post $record) => auth()->user()->can('delete', $record)),
```

## Performance Optimization

### Query Optimization
- Eager load relationships in list pages
- Use `modifyQueryUsing()` for default query modifications
- Implement proper indexes on database
- Use query scopes for common filters
- Avoid N+1 queries

```php
public static function getEloquentQuery(): Builder
{
    return parent::getEloquentQuery()
        ->with(['author', 'category'])
        ->latest();
}
```

### Caching Strategies
- Cache expensive calculations in widgets
- Use query caching for dashboard statistics
- Implement cache invalidation on data changes
- Consider using Redis for better performance

